## About the exhibition

*Tides of Trade* follows the spice, tea and cotton routes that linked ports and peoples from 1600 to 1850. Visitors meet that world through original ship ledgers, navigation instruments and a full-size reconstruction of a cargo hold, where the scale and labor of long-distance trade become something you can stand inside.

At the heart of the exhibition is the 1783 log of the brig *Hesper*, shown publicly for the first time.

Curated by Dr. Rasmus Lindholm, the exhibition brings together 140 objects lent from collections in 12 countries.

